'''3.''' In ''entom.'', the hind body, the posterior one of the three parts of a perfect insect, united with the thorax by a slender connecting portion, and containing the greater part of the digestive apparatus. {{smaller|It is divided into a number of rings or segments, typically eleven (or ten, as in ''Hymenoptera'' and ''Lepidoptera''), on the sides of which are small respiratory stigmata, or spiracles.}}

